# How to Translate Shopify: A Practical Guide

There are several different things you might mean when you want to translate Shopify.

You might want to translate:

- Your storefront
- Shopify Admin
- A Shopify app
- Product content
- Selected text
- A page you are viewing

The best approach depends on what you are trying to translate.

## Translate your Shopify storefront

If you want customers to see your store in multiple languages, you generally need a proper storefront translation solution.

This is different from translating the Shopify Admin that you use as a merchant.

## Translate Shopify Admin

If your goal is to translate the interface you see while managing your store, a browser translation extension can be useful.

Page Translate lets you translate Shopify Admin pages directly in Chrome.

## Translate Shopify apps

Third-party Shopify apps may have their own interfaces.

If an app doesn't support your preferred language, Page Translate can translate the interface while you use it.

## Translate selected text

Sometimes you only need to understand one sentence or setting.

In that case, selecting the text and translating it can be faster than translating the entire page.

## Which Shopify translation method should you use?

It depends on your goal.

| What you want to translate | Suitable approach |
|---|---|
| Storefront content | Store translation solution |
| Product content | Shopify/store translation tools |
| Shopify Admin | Browser translation |
| Third-party Shopify apps | Browser translation |
| One sentence | Selected-text translation |

